WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.066
[music]

2
00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:09.633
[Instructor] So, our game is
just about there.

3
00:00:10.266 --> 00:00:13.700
We have our title screen.
We can click on one of the Buttons.

4
00:00:14.433 --> 00:00:19.066
We have all of these Objects that spawn.
We lose the game.

5
00:00:19.066 --> 00:00:22.600
We can restart, reload our scene.
We've got our Title Screen again.

6
00:00:23.566 --> 00:00:25.533
The last thing we need to do

7
00:00:25.533 --> 00:00:27.866
is actually make these
difficulty Buttons work.

8
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.266
So then our players can
have a little bit of fun.

9
00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:34.900
In our code,
in our difficulty Button Script,

10
00:00:35.133 --> 00:00:40.133
we're going to create a public variable,
so we can assign them immunity.

11
00:00:40.366 --> 00:00:42.400
This will be an integer,

12
00:00:42.766 --> 00:00:45.600
if we're looking for just whole numbers,
and we'll call it difficulty.

13
00:00:47.233 --> 00:00:49.200
Now, in Unity,

14
00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:52.866
if we go to each of our Buttons,
and we scroll down,

15
00:00:52.866 --> 00:00:56.433
you can see that the Difficulty
variable can be set.

16
00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:59.800
So, for Easy,
we'll make the Difficulty 1.

17
00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:04.766
For Medium, 
we'll set the Difficulty to 2,

18
00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:07.600
and for Hard,
we'll set the Difficulty to 3.

19
00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:10.766
Yeah, because each
of these different Buttons

20
00:01:10.766 --> 00:01:12.766
all control there own variables.

21
00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:15.000
It will be really easy to use them.

22
00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:20.633
In our GameManager Script,
we should go down to StartGame(),

23
00:01:20.733 --> 00:01:23.200
since that's what the difficulty
Buttons are using,

24
00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:28.266
and I'll actually pass
in an "int difficulty" parameter,

25
00:01:28.633 --> 00:01:34.600
so that it will use this integer,
and then, lucky for us,

26
00:01:34.733 --> 00:01:38.700
because we actually
made a spawnRate before,

27
00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:42.033
we can actually now use that variable

28
00:01:42.033 --> 00:01:48.166
that we thought of before
to control our difficulty.

29
00:01:49.066 --> 00:01:51.766
So, if we set our spawnRate,

30
00:01:53.533 --> 00:01:56.900
and in this case,
we want our spawns to happen faster,

31
00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:01.666
so we'll divide spawnRate
by the difficulty

32
00:02:01.666 --> 00:02:03.500
that's passed in from our Buttons.

33
00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:06.666
So, when we pass in our difficulty
from our Buttons,

34
00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:09.766
for example, our Easy Button,
our spawnRate here,

35
00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.466
which is currently up to 1 second,

36
00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:16.000
will be divided our Easy difficulty,
which is 1.

37
00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:19.700
So 1 divided by 1,
means our spawnRate will stay at 1.

38
00:02:20.666 --> 00:02:26.000
If we pass in our Medium Button,
then our difficulty becomes 2.

39
00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:32.066
So, it will be 1 divided by 2,
which is 1/2, or 0.5 seconds,

40
00:02:32.666 --> 00:02:37.333
and if we use our Hard difficulty,
it will be divided by 3.

41
00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:42.766
So, 1 divided by 3,
is 1/3, or 0.33 seconds.

42
00:02:43.433 --> 00:02:47.800
If you remember, there's one little bit
of cleaner code that we can write.

43
00:02:48.033 --> 00:02:50.366
So, this is pretty redundant,
right here.

44
00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:54.566
In fact, we can use
the same style of operator

45
00:02:54.566 --> 00:02:57.533
that we used for adding,
and multiplying values

46
00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:01.766
that we were trying to multiply
themselves against other things.

47
00:03:02.066 --> 00:03:06.566
So, if we do "spawnRate /= difficulty;"

48
00:03:06.866 --> 00:03:11.900
this means spawnRate is set to,
spawnRate divided by our difficulty.

49
00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:16.800
Make sure we save that, and now,
in our DifficultyButton Script,

50
00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:19.000
StartGame() is a little annoyed with us,

51
00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:22.633
so we'll pass in,
our difficulty variable.

52
00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:26.166
So, whenever one of the different
Buttons is pressed,

53
00:03:26.466 --> 00:03:28.566
it will send in that difficulty
to StartGame(),

54
00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:30.766
send that information
to our GameManager,

55
00:03:31.133 --> 00:03:34.400
which will then use
that updated spawnRate,

56
00:03:34.733 --> 00:03:36.800
to spawn enemies faster or slower.

57
00:03:37.066 --> 00:03:39.300
So, now we're really communicating

58
00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:42.033
between the different
scripts that we've written.

59
00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:47.866
Very similar to how we were learning
how to use methods,

60
00:03:47.866 --> 00:03:49.833
and parameters before.

61
00:03:49.833 --> 00:03:54.266
If I save this, and now, in Unity,
when I go to my game,

62
00:03:54.866 --> 00:03:59.833
If I press one of the Buttons, so, Easy,
we should see a fairly slow spawnRate.

63
00:04:02.733 --> 00:04:08.866
If I restart, and I press Medium,
it should be a little bit faster.

64
00:04:10.033 --> 00:04:16.266
That's very fast, 
and if I restart one last time,

65
00:04:17.066 --> 00:04:21.133
Hard mode, should spawn
a lot of boxes very fast.

66
00:04:21.133 --> 00:04:26.666
I can't even click on all of them.
So, what you're going to do,

67
00:04:26.666 --> 00:04:29.766
in your DifficultyButton Script,
add a public variable

68
00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.900
that's an integer for your difficulty.

69
00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:35.400
In Unity, select each of your Buttons,

70
00:04:36.066 --> 00:04:38.200
and now that you have
that difficulty variable,

71
00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:43.700
you can set each one to be 1, 2, 3,
however difficult you want it to be.

72
00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:48.166
In our GameManager Script,
if you go to your StartGame(),

73
00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:51.533
pass a parameter
into it using int difficulty,

74
00:04:52.133 --> 00:04:55.266
add a parameter
with our spawnRate variable.

75
00:04:55.633 --> 00:04:58.866
We're going to divide
that by the difficulty.

76
00:04:59.366 --> 00:05:01.300
So, that way our Objects spawn faster,

77
00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:06.300
and then finally in difficulty Button,
under SetDifficulty(),

78
00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:08.800
make sure you pass
the difficulty variable

79
00:05:09.466 --> 00:05:11.166
into your StartGame() method.

80
00:05:12.133 --> 00:05:14.166
Now, it's your turn.

81
00:05:14.766 --> 00:05:16.833
[music]
